1
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:04,670
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:17,430
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

3
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:31,340
[Right yells]

4
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:35,140
[Ivan grunts]

5
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:39,270
[Danji (Tsugai) screams]

6
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:45,310
[LEFT] Right.

7
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,610
What's wrong?

8
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,360
-He has done something bad.
-[RIGHT] Huh?

9
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:51,110
Get out of my way, Right!

10
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:54,320
I told you,
Lady Left's head is mine!

11
00:01:54,450 --> 00:01:55,570
[RIGHT] Huh?

12
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,490
[Ivan grunts]

13
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,500
[grunts]

14
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:01,870
[gasps]

15
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:04,040
♪

16
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:10,960
[Ivan grunting]

17
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:13,260
[gasps] Bastard!

18
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:16,680
I hit his leg!
How is he so agile?

19
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:18,760
[Yuru grunting]

20
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,680
[Right grunts]

21
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:24,640
Dera! Shoot now!

22
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:32,860
[Right grunts]

23
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,910
[Yuru grunts]

24
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,740
[DERA] Yuru!

25
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:46,040
-[LEFT] Uh?
-[Right grunts]

26
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,090
-[RIGHT] Yuru!
-It's just a scratch!

27
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:53,420
-I can still fight.
-You mustn't move.

28
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:54,670
-Stay down!
-So close.

29
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:56,340
[gasps, grunts]

30
00:02:57,380 --> 00:03:00,930
You're kidding.
This guy can redirect bullets?

31
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:05,560
Damn, he disappeared.

32
00:03:06,230 --> 00:03:08,730
[groaning]

33
00:03:09,270 --> 00:03:11,520
[GUARD] That's right,
the warehouse is full of blood.

34
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:13,110
Oh, crap, it's a nightmare.

35
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:16,700
Corpses everywhere.
At least five, maybe 10 dead?

36
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,320
-How should I know?
-[footsteps]

37
00:03:18,410 --> 00:03:19,990
I'm not going in
to count their heads.

38
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:21,910
Send someone as fast as you can.

39
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:23,620
[IVAN] Well, great.

40
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:27,250
[sighs] She hasn't gotten here
to clean up the bodies yet.

41
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:30,790
-[grunts softly]
-Huh? Who're you? No!

42
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:33,050
Buddy! Stop!
You can't go in there!

43
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:35,170
I just called the cops and...

44
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:38,050
Wait, did you do this?

45
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:47,440
Uh, yeah, so...
I just saw a man teleport.

46
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:50,150
[DISPATCHER] What? I...
Sir, are you sure you're okay?

47
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,400
Take a deep breath!

48
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:52,650
EPISODE 20
THE HUNTED AND THE HUNTER

49
00:03:52,730 --> 00:03:55,820
[Bow-Legs and Pigeon-Toes
whimper]

50
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:57,990
[PIGEON-TOES] Help! Help!

51
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:00,620
[SHINGO]
Your daemons control people?

52
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,990
That's one hell
of a messed up pair.

53
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:04,910
Since you came for the boy,

54
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:07,960
I'm guessing you're with
Higashi Village, that right?

55
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:09,500
[bandit grunts]

56
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:10,580
[Shingo grunts]

57
00:04:10,670 --> 00:04:14,500
Hey, you two. Keep a tight grip
on our new friends here.

58
00:04:14,590 --> 00:04:16,960
I ain't about to let 'em
hijack my body.

59
00:04:17,510 --> 00:04:20,760
There's a group of people
gathering on the street outside.

60
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:21,760
[Shingo grunts]

61
00:04:21,850 --> 00:04:23,560
They probably sent
some more of our guys

62
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:25,680
to check on me,
since my phone's broke.

63
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:28,600
I don't like that the Kagemoris
brought Asa, though.

64
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:31,600
We should bounce
before they take our daemons.

65
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:33,440
[ASUMA] Yes, agreed.

66
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,570
My father would have my head

67
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:38,650
if he discovered I've been
acting as a spy on your behalf.

68
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:40,860
The only way to ensure
he doesn't find out

69
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:43,450
-is to kill this man.
-[gasps, trembles]

70
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,410
Be my guest.

71
00:04:45,490 --> 00:04:47,160
[Pigeon-Toes
and Bow-Legs whimper]

72
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:49,330
[BOTH]
No! Please don't hurt him!

73
00:04:49,410 --> 00:04:51,880
No, hold on,
I'll keep my mouth shut.

74
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,830
I swear I will. [trembles]

75
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:56,210
Try not to make a mess,
will you?

76
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:57,840
Blood's a pain to clean up.

77
00:04:57,920 --> 00:05:01,180
I'm begging you!
Can't we cut some kind of deal?

78
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:03,510
-[ASUMA] Sorry, no.
-I'll do anything.

79
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:06,350
Come to think of it,
ain't this your first murder?

80
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:08,980
[ASUMA] That's correct.

81
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:11,600
Though he's not the one
I wish to kill.

82
00:05:11,690 --> 00:05:12,900
[SHINGO] Uh?

83
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:14,360
[gasps]

84
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:15,980
[Shingo gasps, grunts]

85
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:18,610
[ASUMA]
Stay where you are, daemons.

86
00:05:19,150 --> 00:05:20,690
I couldn't show my hand before

87
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:23,030
because you were perched
on the old man's shoulders.

88
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,950
But my moment has arrived.

89
00:05:25,030 --> 00:05:26,660
Aw. Shocked?

90
00:05:26,990 --> 00:05:29,580
I've waited such a long time
for the opportunity

91
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:31,870
to kill you myself,
dearest uncle.

92
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:32,960
Kill me?

93
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:37,090
Fujin! Raijin! What the hell?
Didn't you sense anything?

94
00:05:37,710 --> 00:05:40,510
Yozakura's ability
to conceal their presence

95
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,760
and bloodlust are unmatched.

96
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:45,890
[YOZAKURA] Gonzo, Asa,
and Fuyuki are nearby.

97
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:47,930
I expect they'll arrive
here shortly.

98
00:05:48,010 --> 00:05:49,640
What? It can talk?

99
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,560
You're not going to die yet.

100
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:53,480
We still have
a wealth of information

101
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,560
to extract from you.

102
00:05:54,650 --> 00:05:58,270
[grunts] Fujin!
Blow Yozakura away!

103
00:05:58,360 --> 00:05:59,860
[YOZAKURA]
I would snap your neck

104
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:02,780
before the breeze
even began to stir.

105
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:06,530
Of course, if you try lightning,
you'll be electrocuted as well.

106
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:08,700
What will it be, daemons?

107
00:06:08,790 --> 00:06:11,370
A move against me
will seal your master's fate,

108
00:06:11,450 --> 00:06:15,040
and you'll watch him die
in Yozakura's capable talons.

109
00:06:15,130 --> 00:06:17,630
So, um... Who's on whose team?

110
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:18,960
[SHINGO] You traitor.

111
00:06:19,050 --> 00:06:20,550
You would pull this

112
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,720
after everything
I've invested in you?

113
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:25,180
Poor fool. Listen to you.

114
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,260
You use your money
to control people

115
00:06:27,350 --> 00:06:29,510
and you're surprised
when it doesn't buy you

116
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:30,970
-true loyalty.
-[Shingo grunts]

117
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:34,190
Consider this... What is a clan?

118
00:06:34,270 --> 00:06:36,900
A collection of people
united by something.

119
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:39,310
Those of the Kagemori clan,
servants included,

120
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,900
were rejected because the world
and others viewed us

121
00:06:41,990 --> 00:06:43,490
as useless, different,
and strange.

122
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:45,740
They accepted my mother

123
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:48,120
after the Shingos
treated her terribly.

124
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:51,330
They gave her a home,
a place to belong.

125
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:55,870
You're also family,
but I cannot forgive you.

126
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,250
I never had any intention

127
00:06:57,330 --> 00:06:59,170
of letting you use
the twins' power.

128
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:02,170
Certainly not to destroy
those who saved my mother.

129
00:07:02,550 --> 00:07:05,590
That said, you're not
the only one who has designs

130
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:08,220
on the Kagemori clan, are you?

131
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,760
[Shingo grunting]

132
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:11,970
[ASUMA] It takes more than
one arrogant old man

133
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:14,230
to crush such an organization.

134
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:19,020
Listen well. Your future depends
on how you answer this question.

135
00:07:19,150 --> 00:07:21,190
Somebody has been
guiding your hand.

136
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:24,110
Who are they?

137
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:28,530
[Shingo breathes shakily]

138
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:34,540
What's this?

139
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:37,960
Hey, Ivan! Perfect timing!
Kill this guy!

140
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:40,540
Ah, damn, I see what's going on.

141
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:43,090
I told you not to underestimate
your nephew.

142
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:45,340
Obviously, you didn't take
my advice to heart.

143
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:48,880
Not the time! Gonzo, Asa,
and Fuyuki are here, too!

144
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:50,550
If they catch us, we're screwed!

145
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:51,720
[sword slashes]

146
00:07:51,890 --> 00:07:53,510
Yeah, that's true.

147
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,520
[Shingo and Yozakura groaning]

148
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:57,890
No! Yozakura!

149
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:59,520
[sword slashes]

150
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:03,480
[IVAN]
If Fuyuki's daemons get you,

151
00:08:03,570 --> 00:08:06,360
they'll learn all
the information in your head.

152
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:08,610
Can't let that happen.

153
00:08:16,290 --> 00:08:18,080
Be straight with me, Asuma.

154
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,460
[Asuma breathes shakily]

155
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:22,290
I want to know everything
Shingo told you.

156
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:23,710
[Asuma breathes uneasily]

157
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:27,880
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

158
00:08:29,010 --> 00:08:31,720
[DERA] Crap!
That's not a scratch, damn it!

159
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:33,390
Man, this is bad.

160
00:08:33,890 --> 00:08:36,390
If you show up at a hospital
with a gunshot wound,

161
00:08:36,470 --> 00:08:38,480
they'll have
a ton of questions for you.

162
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,140
Hana is not gonna be happy.

163
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:41,440
[grunts] That hurts!

164
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:43,940
I'm sorry. I didn't know
we were dealing with someone

165
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:46,400
who could deflect rifle bullets
with his swords.

166
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:48,860
It's fine. None of us
could've known.

167
00:08:48,950 --> 00:08:50,570
This wasn't your fault at all.

168
00:08:51,410 --> 00:08:54,490
So was that trick something
his daemons allowed him to do,

169
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:57,500
or is he good enough to have
honed those skills himself?

170
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:59,960
Likely a combination of the two.

171
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,170
Daemons aiding
a master swordsman.

172
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:05,250
Well then, they're extremely
compatible with each other.

173
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:07,170
In any event,
it's bad news for us.

174
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:08,880
That guy was able
to hold his own

175
00:09:08,970 --> 00:09:11,300
while fighting both of you
at the same time.

176
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:12,930
Oh! Hold on.

177
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:16,010
Danji! How do you fare?

178
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:17,850
Hello?

179
00:09:17,930 --> 00:09:19,020
[Danji (Tsugai) gasps]

180
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:21,100
I'm alive! Where the heck is he?

181
00:09:21,850 --> 00:09:23,310
[RIGHT] He got away.

182
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,440
You mind grabbing my leg
while you're down there?

183
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:27,690
I almost forgot
he injured you, too.

184
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:29,190
What can we do to fix you up?

185
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:32,320
[RIGHT] It's nothing for you
to worry about.

186
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:34,370
Just a minor wound
like Left's arm.

187
00:09:34,450 --> 00:09:36,870
We should be as good
as new in no time

188
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:39,200
once you've purchased
a strong adhesive for us.

189
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:42,960
You say that, but the guy
also stabbed you in the heart.

190
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,960
[LEFT] Don't be ridiculous.

191
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:47,170
I'm not human.
I don't have a heart.

192
00:09:47,250 --> 00:09:48,960
What? By that logic,

193
00:09:49,050 --> 00:09:51,470
would you even survive
a headshot?

194
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:52,970
[LEFT] Likely.

195
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:55,680
Is there any injury
that would kill you?

196
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:57,970
-That would kill us?
-[BOTH] Hm?

197
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:01,560
We've never died before,
so we don't know.

198
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:03,940
Okay, yeah, fair point.

199
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,810
[LEFT] We don't understand
death.

200
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:08,440
But his attack
was nothing to scoff at.

201
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:11,240
Completely drained my stamina
in an instant.

202
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,320
What kind of ability was that?

203
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:16,240
Since it KO'd Left and seemed
to kick-start the pervert,

204
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:19,280
my best guess is
some kind of power transference?

205
00:10:19,870 --> 00:10:21,710
KO'd? Kick-started?

206
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:24,120
[DERA] Like a vampire. Hm.

207
00:10:24,210 --> 00:10:27,040
He was thirsty for energy.

208
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:30,380
Whatever the case,
I'll be immobile for a while.

209
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:34,720
The gun is useless against him,
and these two are missing limbs.

210
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,590
We've been taken off the board.

211
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:38,890
Let's leave them
to the Kagemoris.

212
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:41,220
Forgive us, Yuru.

213
00:10:41,310 --> 00:10:42,430
We failed you.

214
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:44,600
He was the best lead you had
on your parents,

215
00:10:44,690 --> 00:10:45,690
and we let him escape.

216
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:48,150
No, I'm the one
who should apologize.

217
00:10:48,230 --> 00:10:49,730
You fought so hard on my behalf

218
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:51,480
and look at the toll it took
on your bodies.

219
00:10:52,070 --> 00:10:53,110
Our current master

220
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:55,030
has such a deep well of kindness
within him

221
00:10:55,110 --> 00:10:57,240
-that it sometimes seems unreal.
-Hm. Hm.

222
00:10:57,370 --> 00:10:58,490
[YURU] Seriously?

223
00:10:58,580 --> 00:11:01,080
What the heck was your
previous master like anyway?

224
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:04,830
[grunts] The pervert may have
gotten away this eve.

225
00:11:04,910 --> 00:11:07,790
But we know the scent
of his blood now.

226
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,840
He won't escape again.

227
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:12,590
Does that mean the two of you
are sticking it out with me?

228
00:11:12,670 --> 00:11:14,590
Of course we are!

229
00:11:14,670 --> 00:11:16,260
Don't you understand?

230
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:19,010
We'll always be by your side,
Master Yuru!

231
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:22,600
That wasn't
terribly nice of you.

232
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:26,020
I was hoping that I would get
the chance to kill him myself.

233
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:29,060
[grunts] I'm sorry, buddy.

234
00:11:29,150 --> 00:11:31,020
Guess I saved you
the trouble, didn't I?

235
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:34,990
Just think,
making a dead body's easy,

236
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:37,110
but cleaning one up sure isn't.

237
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,570
Why get your own hands dirty
when it's easier

238
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:41,990
to just leave it
to the pros like me?

239
00:11:42,370 --> 00:11:44,120
I question the integrity
of advice

240
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,870
given by a man
who would cut down

241
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:48,040
their own employer so easily.

242
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,000
You say that like I was
supposed to have

243
00:11:50,090 --> 00:11:51,880
some special attachment
to Shingo.

244
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:54,420
He was a paycheck.
And all that blood and sweat

245
00:11:54,510 --> 00:11:56,380
I put in for him
more than earned my rate.

246
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:58,220
So you silenced him.

247
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:02,970
I don't suppose he told you
anything before he died?

248
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:06,100
No. You got to him
before he talked.

249
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:08,730
Though I don't believe my uncle
could have done this

250
00:12:08,810 --> 00:12:11,150
without someone else
whispering into his ear.

251
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:14,360
And given how fast
you were to put him down,

252
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:16,490
I suspect you know who that was.

253
00:12:17,990 --> 00:12:19,240
[Ivan sighs]

254
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,530
♪

255
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:34,290
[trembling]

256
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:35,920
[Ivan grunts]

257
00:12:36,010 --> 00:12:37,670
[Asuma breathes shakily]
I'm dead.

258
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:41,640
[Asuma grunts]

259
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:43,600
[Ivan grunts]

260
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:46,100
[grunting]

261
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:48,180
♪

262
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,860
[Ivan breathing heavily]

263
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:01,700
[groans] Holy crap.

264
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:05,030
Left's energy
felt great at first. [grunts]

265
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:07,040
But that kickback is killer.

266
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,750
-[grunting]
-[DAIKYO] Ivan...

267
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:10,750
They're here.

268
00:13:11,830 --> 00:13:14,420
The dangerous people.

269
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:17,300
-[Ivan grunts]
-[MAN 1] Who's this old man?

270
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,090
[man 2 gasps] The Kagemoris!

271
00:13:19,170 --> 00:13:20,800
[screaming]

272
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,260
[Shokyo grunts] I'm sensing
a veritable feast

273
00:13:23,350 --> 00:13:24,430
of daemons here!

274
00:13:24,510 --> 00:13:28,640
Let's take their master's energy
and start another bloodbath!

275
00:13:28,730 --> 00:13:31,270
[IVAN] Nope, not happening
on this leg.

276
00:13:31,350 --> 00:13:32,770
[SHOKYO] From the brat's arrow?

277
00:13:32,850 --> 00:13:35,610
I told you,
just heal it back up!

278
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:37,820
[IVAN] I'll remind you
this is a fresh wound

279
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,900
on top of where
you already stabbed me, idiot.

280
00:13:40,990 --> 00:13:42,910
[SHOKYO]
Oh! That gives me an idea!

281
00:13:42,990 --> 00:13:44,780
If I stab your other leg,

282
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:46,830
that will restore
your body's balance!

283
00:13:46,910 --> 00:13:48,500
Then you can run around again!

284
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:49,540
[Ivan sighs]

285
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:53,290
You're never gonna understand
just how frail humans are.

286
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:57,090
-It's your lucky day, Mr. Asuma.
-[footsteps]

287
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,550
[Ivan groans]

288
00:14:00,010 --> 00:14:01,920
Don't really feel like
dying today,

289
00:14:02,010 --> 00:14:03,630
so it's about time I head out.

290
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:06,510
Besides, aren't you ready
to go back home?

291
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:09,640
We wouldn't want something bad
to happen to Yozakura, would we?

292
00:14:10,310 --> 00:14:11,310
Ta-ta.

293
00:14:11,390 --> 00:14:12,810
-[sword whooshes]
-[glass shatters]

294
00:14:15,310 --> 00:14:17,110
[groans]

295
00:14:24,110 --> 00:14:25,450
♪

296
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:29,990
[Ivan grunts]

297
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,670
[door opens]

298
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:39,380
Whoa! This is quite the scene!

299
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:40,590
What happened here?

300
00:14:40,670 --> 00:14:42,380
[gasps] Asuma, your arm!

301
00:14:42,470 --> 00:14:44,090
Is the cut serious, son?

302
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:46,140
[ASUMA] Forgive me, Father.

303
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:49,260
I failed to capture
my uncle alive.

304
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:51,350
Oh, Shingo.

305
00:14:51,430 --> 00:14:53,520
Were you the one who did him in?

306
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:56,230
[ASUMA] No.
There was a falling out.

307
00:14:56,310 --> 00:14:58,610
Or rather,
they didn't want him talking.

308
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:01,400
This is the doing
of Ivan Yosano.

309
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:04,740
Yosano? I recall you told us

310
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:07,200
about a Daemon Wielder
Shingo recently hired

311
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:08,660
with dual katanas.

312
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:09,910
[Asa gasps]

313
00:15:09,990 --> 00:15:12,620
Sir, there was a man outside
with katanas!

314
00:15:12,700 --> 00:15:15,750
I should have used Break
to try to capture him.

315
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,380
My apologies, Fuyuki.

316
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,630
Not even the relics remain
of his daemons.

317
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:23,800
You can't extract anything.

318
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:26,970
I learned my uncle had
someone behind the scenes

319
00:15:27,050 --> 00:15:28,800
who was feeding him information,

320
00:15:28,890 --> 00:15:31,260
but he died
before I found out who.

321
00:15:31,350 --> 00:15:32,640
I have failed.

322
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:35,890
You shouldn't concern yourself
with that in your present state.

323
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:38,100
Let's stop your bleeding.

324
00:15:38,190 --> 00:15:39,230
[Asuma gasps]

325
00:15:39,310 --> 00:15:43,030
The man from Higashi Village
we captured got away, too.

326
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:49,490
[Bow-Legs and Pigeon-Toes
squealing]

327
00:15:49,570 --> 00:15:51,530
[line ringing]

328
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:03,750
[WOMAN] Hey, hey, hey, hey!
How's my big ol' cutie doing?

329
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:05,010
[Ivan sighs]

330
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:08,050
[IVAN] Mineyama, where are you?

331
00:16:08,130 --> 00:16:09,760
At the warehouse, duh!

332
00:16:10,510 --> 00:16:12,600
[IVAN] The bodies were
still there a minute ago.

333
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,100
Hurry up and do your job.

334
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:15,640
[MINEYAMA] Aw, I'm so sorry
for being late!

335
00:16:15,730 --> 00:16:18,770
I mean, this place is so big.
I got lost!

336
00:16:19,560 --> 00:16:22,230
But no worries,
I'm taking care of it right now!

337
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:24,820
Come on, I already said
I was sorry, didn't I?

338
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:25,990
I mean, I can't help it

339
00:16:26,070 --> 00:16:27,700
if my cram school
lets me out late.

340
00:16:29,410 --> 00:16:32,160
And, like, you killed
so many people.

341
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:34,910
It's a lot of work to clean
all that up for you.

342
00:16:34,990 --> 00:16:37,370
Of course, my pair
is always delighted to do it!

343
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:38,960
Huh?

344
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,170
Are you telling me
every one of these people

345
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,670
was from Higashi Village?

346
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:45,210
I've never fed my buddies
mountain meat before.

347
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:48,420
Anyway, where can I find you
when I'm finished up?

348
00:17:01,350 --> 00:17:02,690
There!

349
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:04,520
Job well done.

350
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:06,440
♪

351
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:07,690
Uh?

352
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:09,950
-[whimpering]
-What's wrong, mister?

353
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:11,910
If you're starting
to see weird things,

354
00:17:11,990 --> 00:17:13,580
it's probably
'cause you're tired.

355
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:14,870
You should go home and sleep.

356
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:17,870
[whimpering]

357
00:17:17,950 --> 00:17:19,040
♪

358
00:17:19,290 --> 00:17:21,620
[officer 1 sighs] The call said
there was a massacre

359
00:17:21,710 --> 00:17:23,340
in this warehouse, right?

360
00:17:25,050 --> 00:17:26,840
I mean, forget bodies.

361
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,670
I don't even see
a drop of blood.

362
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:29,970
Me neither.

363
00:17:30,050 --> 00:17:30,970
Uh?

364
00:17:31,590 --> 00:17:33,760
Whoa, there's a hole
in the roof.

365
00:17:33,850 --> 00:17:35,470
[OFFICER 1] What the hell?

366
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,220
We've been trying
for a few minutes,

367
00:17:37,310 --> 00:17:38,560
but we can't get him
to calm down.

368
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:41,190
[GUARD] But I... I saw it.
[cries]

369
00:17:41,270 --> 00:17:43,730
Relax, sir. We're just trying
to understand, 'kay?

370
00:17:43,810 --> 00:17:45,110
[GUARD] You don't get it!

371
00:17:45,190 --> 00:17:47,940
You guys think I'm crazy!
But I saw it!

372
00:17:48,030 --> 00:17:51,320
They were all dead.
Then a young girl showed up.

373
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:56,080
She rolled up all the bodies
into a ball and left.

374
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:57,330
[OFFICER] Uh...

375
00:17:57,410 --> 00:18:00,620
[guard cries]
Just tell me, officers,

376
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:03,330
have I really
gone off the deep end after all?

377
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:04,960
[cries]

378
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:06,420
[footsteps]

379
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:08,340
[MINEYAMA] Oh, Master Ivan!

380
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,590
Ivan, sweetie!

381
00:18:10,670 --> 00:18:11,840
Mm? [chuckles]

382
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,760
There you are!

383
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:15,350
Guess who's here?

384
00:18:15,470 --> 00:18:17,560
Ugh, don't yell.
My head is killing me.

385
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:18,890
Be still, my heart!

386
00:18:18,970 --> 00:18:20,850
The big strong man
needs my help!

387
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:22,980
[SHOKYO] Ivan, can I kill her?

388
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:25,560
[IVAN] For once, we feel
the same way, Shokyo.

389
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:29,030
Oh, did you do the life energy
transfer thing?

390
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:32,070
Yeah. I tried to recover
a bit off of Left.

391
00:18:32,150 --> 00:18:34,490
Whoa! You drained
a freakin' god!

392
00:18:34,570 --> 00:18:35,910
Bet that felt wild.

393
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:39,040
Yeah. It feels like
I went and chugged

394
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:41,370
a bucket full of energy drinks
all at once.

395
00:18:41,450 --> 00:18:43,160
Ah, crap.

396
00:18:43,250 --> 00:18:45,920
The strain on my heart
is getting to be too much.

397
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,880
[grunts] I'll be out of action
for a while.

398
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:51,630
Wait, if you can't move,
then this is my chance!

399
00:18:51,710 --> 00:18:52,880
Don't worry yourself!

400
00:18:52,970 --> 00:18:55,800
I'm ready to give you
mouth to mouth! [panting]

401
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,850
-Back off, pervert.
-[chuckles excitedly]

402
00:18:59,010 --> 00:19:00,140
Yeah, or what?

403
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:02,850
You couldn't even beat Left
let alone kill Yuru,

404
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:06,440
so you have got nothing
to show for your efforts.

405
00:19:07,150 --> 00:19:11,070
Don't be so sure.
Yuru's gonna come after me.

406
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,530
I'll get my second chance
before long.

407
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:16,200
Aw, sounds like the two of you
are in love!

408
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:18,450
Be careful or I'll get jealous.

409
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:20,740
Well, good luck out there.

410
00:19:20,830 --> 00:19:23,200
You'd better stay safe,
'cause I'd just hate

411
00:19:23,290 --> 00:19:26,210
to have to bring you back to
Nishino Village as a meatball!

412
00:19:26,830 --> 00:19:28,210
[ASA] Brother...

413
00:19:28,290 --> 00:19:29,960
[whimpers]

414
00:19:30,050 --> 00:19:31,670
You got shot?

415
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:34,880
Yeah. Dera shot my shoulder
with his "rifle" thingy.

416
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:36,680
I'll kill you, Dera!

417
00:19:36,760 --> 00:19:39,390
Context! Give her the context!

418
00:19:39,470 --> 00:19:41,430
[ASA] I distinctly remember
back at the manor,

419
00:19:41,510 --> 00:19:42,930
you said you'd take care of him!

420
00:19:43,020 --> 00:19:45,310
[DERA] I'm sorry! Really, I am!

421
00:19:45,390 --> 00:19:47,940
[ASA] And you're no better!
What're all those muscles for

422
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:49,520
if you can't keep
my brother safe?

423
00:19:49,610 --> 00:19:51,820
-Fair point.
-Apologies.

424
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,070
[ASA] Oh, I knew it.

425
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:55,320
The Kagemoris should've
taken him in after all!

426
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,320
We can't trust Higashi Village!

427
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,950
Just look at this lineup
you had!

428
00:19:59,030 --> 00:20:01,580
Three powerhouses, and you still
couldn't protect Yuru!

429
00:20:01,660 --> 00:20:03,620
-And as for you!
-[gasps]

430
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,410
I'm so sorry.

431
00:20:06,660 --> 00:20:07,920
[Asa sighs softly]

432
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,380
♪

433
00:20:13,550 --> 00:20:15,340
[both breathe uneasily]

434
00:20:16,510 --> 00:20:18,800
[ASA] I'll let you out
when I'm done working.

435
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:23,220
[ASA (FAKE)] How long
have we been trapped in here?

436
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:26,140
[gasps]

437
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:28,890
Huh? Where'd she go?

438
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:33,150
Wait. Does this mean
she's letting us out?

439
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:37,570
[Asa (fake) gasps]

440
00:20:39,070 --> 00:20:40,160
Brother.

441
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:42,160
You're here.

442
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:46,830
[AZAMI] Uh? [whimpers]

443
00:20:46,910 --> 00:20:48,250
Who are you?

444
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:49,920
-[DERA] Hey! Azami.
-Uh?

445
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,790
-Glad you're all right, kiddo.
-[AZAMI] Huh?

446
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:56,510
Oh! Mr. Dera?
What happened to your beard?

447
00:20:56,590 --> 00:20:59,050
And, um... What is this place?

448
00:20:59,130 --> 00:21:01,430
[cries] Nothing here
makes any sense to me!

449
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:03,720
Please, can I go back home?

450
00:21:03,810 --> 00:21:06,020
Try to relax, young lady.
It's fine.

451
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:08,730
Those scary men
aren't here anymore.

452
00:21:08,810 --> 00:21:11,020
Get away! You're scary, too!

453
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:13,310
I can tell
your smile isn't real!

454
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,110
-[Azami cries]
-[Gonzo sighs]

455
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:18,150
[RIGHT] Come now,
calm down, lass!

456
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:20,360
We're here to make sure
you stay safe!

457
00:21:20,450 --> 00:21:21,410
[AZAMI] Huh?

458
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:22,990
Uh...

459
00:21:23,070 --> 00:21:26,330
Oh, right. I forgot,
you can't see us.

460
00:21:27,370 --> 00:21:28,870
Remember from before?

461
00:21:28,950 --> 00:21:30,830
We had met in Higashi Village!

462
00:21:30,910 --> 00:21:32,170
[AZAMI] Uh?

463
00:21:32,290 --> 00:21:33,420
[squeaks]

464
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,590
[thuds]

465
00:21:34,670 --> 00:21:38,090
Uh-oh. She has lost
consciousness again.

466
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:39,720
Still kinda hurts, you know!

467
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:43,140
Hold on. If Azami's the only one
who came out,

468
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:49,730
then inside, Yuru, Danji
and both Asas are duking it out.

469
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:52,520
That won't be pretty.

470
00:21:54,900 --> 00:21:57,320
[♪ closing theme song playing]

471
00:23:26,610 --> 00:23:27,910
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

472
00:23:27,990 --> 00:23:29,700
[ASA (FAKE)] I'm so sorry.

473
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:33,120
It was wrong. I knew that,
but I kept doing it.

474
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:36,000
[KYOKA] In the face
of unimaginable power,

475
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:38,130
people lose their humanity.

476
00:23:38,210 --> 00:23:39,790
EPISODE 21: ZASHIKI-WARASHI
AND HIGASHI VILLAGE
